# Database

SQLite (`sqlite3`, WAL) and PostgreSQL (`psycopg`) share one schema.

- Add a numbered pair: `infra/db/migrations/00N_description.sql` and `00N_description.pg.sql`.
- Bump the `v ==` assertion in `tests/unit/db/test_db_pool.py`.
- Unreleased work on `develop` folds into the current unreleased `00N`. Cut `00N+1` only after that version has shipped, or when a database already at `N` would skip the change.
- `_schema_version` is an applied-migration watermark. `migrate.py` helpers stay idempotent and equivalent to the SQL pair. Do not re-apply a RENAME rebuild just to clamp the watermark.

Resource tables (`agents`, `channels`, `threads`, `cron_jobs`, …):

| Column | Role |
|--------|------|
| `id` | Integer surrogate PK |
| `{entity}_id` | Public string UNIQUE (ULID). APIs and foreign keys use this |

Child rows store the string id and `REFERENCES parent({entity}_id)`. Repos map `row.id` to the public string; keep the integer as `row.pk`.

Do not force that shape onto `users` (integer `user_id`), name-keyed config, append-only logs, KV (`settings`, `secrets`), 1:1 extensions, or ephemeral rows (`sso_login_states`).

Repos are SQL-only: import `infra/db/_base` and `infra/utils/`, not agents, gateway, or API.
